{"kind":"request","text":"Security R8 (6dd06d03 sections 3.1 and 5): screens off the room origin, and the page key out of localStorage.\n\nToday the room page keeps the member's signing secret in localStorage (apps/room/page/src/main.ts:64-83). Trusted package screens are served from the same origin under script-src 'self' (packages/scope/src/applications/route.ts:1-3, :19). So any trusted publisher's script can read the secret.\n\nWork:\n1. Serve application screens from the sandbox origin: the inguz.space shim Worker, route *.inguz.space/*. The zone is active, and the shim is not deployed. The room origin stops serving screen assets, and answers a screen request with a refusal or a redirect to the sandbox origin.\n2. Move the page's signing key to a non-extractable WebCrypto key in IndexedDB, as the Counter does. On first load, an existing localStorage secret becomes a non-extractable key, and the page then deletes the localStorage copy. The member keeps the same key and identity.\n3. Use one key store for this and for the sign-in URL page route of request abe69eeb.\n\nWitnesses:\n- The room origin does not serve a screen asset.\n- After migration, localStorage on the room origin holds no secret, and exportKey on the page key fails.\n- A member with a localStorage secret keeps the same key ID after migration and can still act.\n- A screen on the sandbox origin works for the existing grow and lending packages.\n\nThe planner deploys the shim and the page after review. Closes 3.1.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 4 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Screens served from inguz.space; non-extractable page key with migration; closes 3.1. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}